# Constraint-Driven Folder Architecture

## Core Principle

A profile is a **named set of constraints AND query functions**. The name is arbitrary. The system never checks the name — it reads properties and calls functions.

- **Capabilities** answer: "Can this folder do X?" (create, rename, delete, favorite, recover, etc.)
- **Query functions** answer: "What are this folder's children/notes?" The profile carries the implementation. The system just calls it.
- **View properties** answer: "How does this folder render?" (icon, section, children expandable)

---

## Part 1: Profile Shape

### File: `src/lib/stores/domain/profiles.ts` (new shared module)

The profile type:

```
type FolderProfileConfig = {
    // === View ===
    iconName: FolderIcon;
    section: 'views' | 'folders';
    sectionIndex?: number;
    childrenExpandable: boolean;
    showDeletedChildren: boolean;

    // === Capabilities (constraints) ===
    capabilities: SidebarCapabilities;
    canCreateNote: boolean;

    // === Query functions ===
    resolveChildFolderIds: (item: FolderItem, store: FolderStoreLike) => FolderID[];
    resolveNotes: (folderId: FolderID, allNotes: NoteItem[]) => NoteItem[];
}
```

### Key design decision: query functions receive data, not stores

`resolveChildFolderIds` receives `(item, store)` so it can query whatever it needs.
`resolveNotes` receives `(folderId, allNotes)` — the full notes array, and returns the filtered subset.

The system never interprets what the profile is doing. It just calls the function and uses the result.

### Profile definitions

**trash**
```
resolveChildFolderIds: (_item, store) => store.trashItems
resolveNotes: (_folderId, allNotes) => allNotes.filter(n => n.deletedAt != null)
canCreateNote: false
capabilities: { create: false, rename: false, delete: false, emptyTrash: true, ... }
section: 'views', sectionIndex: 0
childrenExpandable: false, showDeletedChildren: true
```

**favorites**
```
resolveChildFolderIds: (_item, store) => {
    const result = [];
    for (const [id, folder] of store.folders.entries()) {
        if (folder.isFavorite && folder.deletedAt == null
            && resolveProfile(folder).capabilities.favorite) {
            result.push(id);
        }
    }
    return result;
}
resolveNotes: (_folderId, allNotes) =>
    allNotes.filter(n => n.isFavorite === true && n.deletedAt == null)
canCreateNote: false
capabilities: { create: false, rename: false, delete: false, favorite: false, ... }
section: 'views', sectionIndex: 1
childrenExpandable: false, showDeletedChildren: false
```

**home**
```
resolveChildFolderIds: (_item, store) =>
    store.items.filter(id => {
        const f = store.findItemById(id);
        return f && f.deletedAt == null && resolveProfile(f).section === 'folders';
    })
resolveNotes: (_folderId, allNotes) =>
    allNotes.filter(n => n.folderId == null && n.deletedAt == null)
canCreateNote: true
capabilities: { create: true, rename: false, delete: false, favorite: false, ... }
section: 'views', sectionIndex: 2
childrenExpandable: true, showDeletedChildren: false
```

> [!NOTE]
> Home's `resolveChildFolderIds` returns root-level folders whose profile has `section === 'folders'`. This is a property check, not a name check. Home's `resolveNotes` returns notes with `folderId === null`. So when a note is recovered to `folderId: null`, it naturally appears under Home.

**regular**
```
resolveChildFolderIds: (item, _store) => item.items ?? []
resolveNotes: (folderId, allNotes) =>
    allNotes.filter(n => (n.folderId ?? 'root') === folderId && n.deletedAt == null)
canCreateNote: true
capabilities: { create: true, rename: true, delete: true, favorite: true, ... }
section: 'folders'
childrenExpandable: true, showDeletedChildren: false
```

**deleted**
```
resolveChildFolderIds: () => []
resolveNotes: (folderId, allNotes, store) => {
    // existing subtree logic for viewing a deleted folder's notes
}
canCreateNote: false
capabilities: { create: false, recover: true, permanentDelete: true, ... }
section: null (never appears as a root section item)
childrenExpandable: false, showDeletedChildren: false
```

### Profile resolution function

```
function resolveProfile(item: FolderItem): FolderProfileConfig {
    if (item.deletedAt != null) return PROFILE_REGISTRY['deleted'];
    return PROFILE_REGISTRY[item.profile ?? 'regular'];
}
```

This is the ONLY branching. Everything else is a function call or property read.

