## Part 7: Test Changes

### Mock data updates

All test files replace `type: 'trash'` → `profile: 'trash'`, `type: 'system'` → `profile: 'favorites'` / `profile: 'home'`. This is a data contract update, not a logic change.

The `id: 'notes'` → `id: 'home'` rename (done by user) is carried into test mocks.

### New test: Name independence

Create a folder with `profile: 'favorites'` but `id: 'lovey-dovy'`, `title: 'Things I Love'`. Verify:
- It appears in the views section (profile.section === 'views')
- It shows the star icon (profile.iconName)
- Its children are the favorited folders (profile.resolveChildFolderIds)
- Its notes are the favorite notes (profile.resolveNotes)
- Context menu is empty (capabilities all false)

This proves zero code checks the name.

